# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DUET — repository hygiene
#
# The working tree carries ~3.4 GB of data and intermediate results. None of it
# belongs on GitHub: the inputs are public and re-downloadable (see README), and
# every table here is reproducible from the scripts. What IS tracked from
# results/ is the small stuff a reader wants without re-running anything:
# the summaries, the concordance tables, the null/simulation scores, and figures.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- never, under any circumstances ---
*codex*
*Codex*
*CODEX*

# --- data (public, re-downloadable; see README for provenance) ---
data/
*.h5ad
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.rds
*.tar
*.loom

# --- benchmark working directories (regenerate with bench_mast_*.py / .R) ---
bench/
**/_mast_work/
_tmp_*/

# --- backups made during the July 2026 refactor ---
code_backup_*/
results_backup_*/

# --- exploratory subproject, superseded by the three-dataset comparison ---
SmallComapre/

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R ---
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# --- results: NOT tracked ---
# Code only for now. Everything under results*/ is derived from data that is
# either unpublished (the pancreas/PDAC object) or re-downloadable (Kang,
# Crowell, the muscat simulation), and every table is reproducible from the
# scripts. Revisit when the preprint goes up.
results/
results_kang/
results_crowell/
results_sim/
results_null/
de_*_all_celltypes.csv
comparison_per_gene.csv
consensus_genes.csv
mast_all_celltypes*.csv
*.log

# --- os / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
